# Moonstone UI

This project uses [@jahia/moonstone](https://github.com/Jahia/moonstone) as its design system. Do not add other component libraries.

## Defaults

| Need          | Use                                                                      |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Buttons       | `Button` (`label`, `variant`, `onClick`; use `aria-pressed` for toggles) |
| Text / titles | `Typography` (`variant` such as `title`)                                 |
| Small labels  | `Chip`                                                                   |
| Icons         | Moonstone icon components (e.g. `ChevronDown`, `Folder`)                 |

Import from a single entry:

```tsx
import { Button, Typography } from "@jahia/moonstone";
```

Match existing components: `src/components/Toolbar.tsx`, `TreeRow.tsx`, `NodeDetails.tsx`.

## Layout and styling

- Use existing CSS classes in `src/app.css` for layout (e.g. `toolbar`, tree rows). Moonstone covers controls and typography, not full page layout.
- Prefer Moonstone `Button` / `Typography` over raw `<button>` or unstyled text for new UI.

## Exceptions

- **Tree a11y**: Keep WAI-ARIA tree roles, roving tabindex, and keyboard handling as custom markup in `ContentTree` / `TreeRow`; do not replace the tree with a generic Moonstone widget unless the task explicitly asks for it.
- **Tests** (`src/tests/**`): Use Testing Library; no requirement to render Moonstone in tests unless asserting UI copy or roles.

## Out of scope

- No new UI dependencies (MUI, Radix kits, shadcn, etc.).
- `vite.config.ts` already inlines `@jahia/moonstone`; leave that as-is unless build breaks.
